ification says Schedule 40, ask for the wall thickness in millimetres per size and compare it with what is delivered."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can uPVC pipe be used for hot water?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. uPVC softens and loses strength as temperature rises. Hot-water lines need CPVC, PPR or a metal system. Using uPVC on hot water is one of the most common causes of premature pipe failure."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can PVC pipe be used underground?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes — uPVC is widely used for buried water mains and drainage. It needs proper bedding and backfill, and where heavy traffic loads are expected the correct pipe class and surround must be used."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do you supply PVC pipe outside Karachi?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, we deliver across Pakistan. Send your delivery location with the enquiry and we will quote freight and lead time with the pipe price."}}]}
</script>

